We need to refer to initial size before insertion: \old(this.size()).

Valid index condition: index >= 0 && index <= \old(this.size()) (since insertion at size is allowed, adds at end). Also role != null (but method throws if null, but condition includes). So premise: index>=0 && index<=\old(this.size()) && role != null.

Conclusion: for all int i; 0 <= i && i < index; the element at that position after insertion (this.get(i)) equals the old element at same position ( \old(this.get(i)) ) or both are null? The comment says "remains unchanged or continues to be null". That suggests if old element was null, after insertion it may still be null (unchanged). So essentially this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i)). Since unchanged includes null case. So we can assert equality.

Thus assert: (index>=0 && index<=\old(this.size()) && role != null) => \forall int i; 0<=i && i<index; this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i)))? Need to handle null. Use == for reference equality? In previous examples they used .equals for objects. To handle null, we can use (this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i))) . That works for null and same object reference.

Thus final assert:

assert (index>=0 && index<=\old(this.size()) && role != null) => \forall int i; 0<=i && i<index; this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i));

